                                "text": "A series of public-relations disasters, culminating in the botched dismissal of popular announcer Ernie Harwell, irritated its most loyal followers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "63dfd2bf-6d66-450a-882a-152112bd8ab6",
                                "sense_id": "63d2e9b0-aa12-322d-98d5-c6aa9e7dd11d",
                                "text": "She was sixty when she died from some kind of botched surgery."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f1a812d-65e3-4d2b-8eee-4893427f5bc9",
                                "sense_id": "63d2e9b0-aa12-322d-98d5-c6aa9e7dd11d",
                                "text": "Expert headsmen were highly prized—by the victim most of all—since a botched blow could result in enormous pain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0fbfbfa6-2a53-4320-8ae1-a76bb8c23acf",
                                "sense_id": "63d2e9b0-aa12-322d-98d5-c6aa9e7dd11d",
                                "text": "The US government's first attempt to map carbon dioxide in Earth's atmosphere from space ended early on Tuesday after a botched satellite launch from California, officials said. (Reuters, février 2009)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
